.Dd October 3, 2026
.Dt POC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm poc
.Nd the Peaseblossom Oberon-2 compiler
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar option ...
.Op Fl build
.Ar file
.Nm
.Op Ar option ...
.Fl check Ar file
.Nm
.Op Ar option ...
.Fl compile Ar file ...
.Nm
.Op Ar option ...
.Fl library Ar name Ar file ...
.Nm
.Op Ar option ...
.Fl install-library Ar name
.Nm
.Op Ar option ...
.Fl emit-interface | show-interface | emit-llvm-ir
.Ar file
.Nm
.Op Ar option ...
.Fl print-import-path | print-library-path
.Nm
.Op Fl target Ar triple
.Op Fl O2 | OC
.Fl version
.Nm
.Fl help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
compiles programs written in Oberon-2, as the report
.Em The Programming Language Oberon-2
by H. M\(:ossenb\(:ock and N. Wirth defines it, with a few extensions
.Pq Fl strict No turns them off .
It compiles through LLVM, running
.Xr clang 1
to compile and link, and its runtime library has the modules of the Vishap
Oberon compiler
.Pq voc
with their interfaces.
.Pp
A
.Ar file
is a module's source.
Its name need not match the module's; by custom it is
.Pa Module.Mod .
The modules it imports are found in libraries, then as sources or compiled
modules on the import path
.Pq see Sx MODULES AND LIBRARIES .
.Pp
Options come before the command; when an option is given twice, the later
one wins.
.Nm
says nothing when it succeeds in building a program, a library or a
compilation.
It writes each error as
.Ar file : Ns Ar line : Ns Ar column : No error : Ar what ,
on the standard error, and then their number.
.Ss Commands
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar file , Fl build Ar file
Build a program:
compile the module in
.Ar file
and each module it imports that no library has, each to
.Pa Module.sym ,
.Pa Module.ll
and
.Pa Module.o ,
and link them with the libraries into an executable named after the
module, in the current directory.
.It Fl check Ar file
Check the module against the interfaces of the modules it imports, and
write nothing but
.Dq semantic OK
or the errors.
Imports come only from libraries and
.Pa .sym
files, and are never compiled.
The module is checked for the target a build would use:
.Fl target Ns 's,
or else the host's.
.It Fl compile Ar file ...
Compile each module to
.Pa .sym ,
.Pa .ll
and
.Pa .o ,
and link nothing.
A module's
.Pa .sym
and
.Pa .o
can then stand in for its source.
.It Fl library Ar name Ar file ...
Build the library
.Ar name
from the modules: in
.Ar output-dir Ns Pa / Ns Ar triple Ns Pa / Ns Ar model Ns Pa / ,
the archive
.Pa lib Ns Ar name Ns Pa .a ,
the shared library
.Pa lib Ns Ar name Ns Pa .so ,
each module's
.Pa .sym ,
.Pa .ll ,
.Pa .o
and
.Pa .owner ,
and the manifest
.Ar name Ns Pa .library .
.It Fl install-library Ar name
Copy the library
.Ar name
from the library path into
.Ar output-dir Ns Pa / Ns Ar triple Ns Pa / Ns Ar model Ns Pa / ,
or without
.Fl output-dir
into
.Nm Ns 's
own library directory.
.It Fl emit-interface Ar file
Write the module's interface,
.Pa Module.sym .
.It Fl show-interface Ar file
Print the module's interface on the standard output.
.It Fl emit-llvm-ir Ar file
Write the module's LLVM IR,
.Pa Module.ll .
.It Fl print-import-path , Fl print-library-path
Print the import path or the library path as the options before it leave
it.
.It Fl version
Print the version of
.Nm
and the commit it was built from, the target and size model, and the
version of
.Xr clang 1 .
.It Fl help , Fl h , Fl -help
Print a summary of the commands and options on the standard output.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
with no arguments lists every command and option on the standard error,
including commands for testing
.Nm
itself:
.Fl dump-tokens ,
.Fl check-syntax ,
.Fl dump-layout ,
.Fl dump-llvm-types
and
.Fl dump-nested .
.Ss Options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl o Ar exe
Name the executable
.Ar exe .
.It Fl O2 , Fl OC
The size model.
Under
.Fl O2 ,
the default,
.Vt SHORTINT ,
.Vt INTEGER
and
.Vt LONGINT
have 8, 16 and 32 bits; under
.Fl OC ,
16, 32 and 64.
.Vt HUGEINT
has 64 bits and
.Vt SET
32 under both.
A program and the modules it imports share one model.
.It Fl import-path Ar dir
Add
.Ar dir
to the directories searched for modules.
May be repeated.
.It Fl clear-import-path
Empty the import path, including the directories of
.Ev POC_IMPORT_PATH .
.It Fl library-path Ar dir
Add
.Ar dir
to the directories searched for libraries.
May be repeated.
.It Fl clear-library-path
Search no library directory: neither
.Fl library-path Ns 's
before it,
.Ev POC_LIBRARY_PATH Ns 's ,
nor
.Nm Ns 's
own.
.It Fl output-dir Ar dir
Write
.Pa .sym ,
.Pa .ll
and
.Pa .o
files, and libraries, in
.Ar dir ,
making it if it is not there.
.It Fl target Ar triple
Compile for the LLVM target
.Ar triple
instead of the host, as far as
.Xr clang 1
can; linking needs the target's C library.
.It Fl opt Ar level
Have
.Xr clang 1
optimize at
.Ar level :
0, 1, 2, 3, s, z or g.
The default is 2, and 0 on 32-bit x86, whose reals are the x87's.
.It Fl g
Generate debugging information for
.Xr gdb 1
and
.Xr lldb 1 ,
and look for each library's debugging copy first.
Best with
.Fl opt Cm 0
or
.Fl opt Cm g .
.It Fl trap-location
Begin each trap's message with the file, line and column of the trap, and
end it with the procedure's name.
.It Fl trap-heap-exhausted
Make a
.Fn NEW
that the heap cannot satisfy a trap, exit status 11, instead of leaving the
pointer NIL.
.It Fl range-checks
Make
.Fn SHORT
of an integer, and
.Fn CHR ,
of a value that does not fit a trap, exit status 14.
.It Fl strict
Accept in the module named only the language of the report: each of
.Nm Ns 's
extensions is an error there.
The modules it imports are not checked.
.It Fl static
Link a fully static executable.
.It Fl shared-libraries
Link the libraries' shared objects instead of their archives.
.It Fl link Ar arg
Pass
.Ar arg
to the link, such as
.Fl l Ns Ar lib
or
.Fl L Ns Ar dir .
May be repeated.
.It Fl c-flag Ar arg
Pass
.Ar arg
to
.Xr clang 1
when it compiles a module's part in C,
.Pa Module.c
beside
.Pa Module.Mod .
May be repeated.
.It Fl lto
Compile to LLVM bitcode, and optimize the whole program when it is linked.
.It Fl verbose
Print each command
.Nm
runs.
.El
.Sh MODULES AND LIBRARIES
A module named in an
.Ic IMPORT
is taken from the first of:
.Bl -enum
.It
a library on the library path;
.It
.Pa Module.Mod
or
.Pa Module.mod
in the current directory, then in each directory of the import path;
.It
.Pa Module.sym
with
.Pa Module.o
or
.Pa Module.ll ,
searched for in the same way.
.El
.Pp
The import path is the directories of
.Ev POC_IMPORT_PATH ,
then those of each
.Fl import-path .
The library path is the directories of each
.Fl library-path ,
then those of
.Ev POC_LIBRARY_PATH ,
then
.Nm Ns 's
own library directory,
.Pa ../lib/poc
from the directory of the
.Nm
executable.
A library is in the subdirectory
.Ar triple Ns Pa / Ns Ar model
of one of them, where
.Ar model
is
.Li O2
or
.Li OC ,
with
.Li -g
appended for its debugging copy.
.Pp
Each module's object records the interfaces its imports had when it was
compiled, so a program links only if all its modules agree.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev POC_IMPORT_PATH
Directories, separated by colons, searched for modules before those of
.Fl import-path .
.It Ev POC_LIBRARY_PATH
Directories, separated by colons, searched for libraries after those of
.Fl library-path .
.It Ev PATH
Where
.Nm
finds
.Xr clang 1 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa Module.sym
A module's interface, as Oberon text.
.It Pa Module.ll
A module's LLVM IR.
.It Pa Module.o
A module's object.
.It Pa Module.c
A module's part in C, compiled and linked with it.
.It Pa ../lib/poc/ Ns Ar triple Ns Pa / Ns Ar model Ns Pa /
The runtime library,
.Li poc-rtl ,
relative to the directory of the
.Nm
executable.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when it did what was asked, and 1 when it reported an error or its
arguments were wrong.
.Pp
A program
.Nm
built exits 0 when its main module's body ends,
.Ar n
after
.Fn HALT n ,
and on a trap, after writing what happened on the standard error:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 2
an index out of range
.It 3
no matching
.Ic CASE
label
.It 4
a NIL pointer dereference, or a call of a NIL procedure value
.It 5
a type guard that failed
.It 6
no matching
.Ic WITH
guard
.It 7
a length of a dynamic array that is not positive, or too large
.It 8
.Fn ENTIER
of a value that does not fit a
.Vt LONGINT
.It 9
an open array assigned to an array too short for it
.It 10
.Fn ASSERT
failed
.It 11
heap exhausted
.Pq with Fl trap-heap-exhausted
.It 12
a function procedure that reached its end without
.Ic RETURN
.It 13
a record assigned to a variable whose dynamic type extends its static type
.It 14
.Fn SHORT
or
.Fn CHR
out of range
.Pq with Fl range-checks
.It 99
a file error the runtime module
.Li Files
cannot return
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Build and run a program:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ poc Hello.Mod
$ ./Hello
.Ed
.Pp
Build a program from modules in
.Pa ../lib ,
under the larger size model, with debugging information:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ poc -OC -g -opt 0 -import-path ../lib -o main Main.Mod
.Ed
.Pp
Check a module against the report alone:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ poc -strict -check Counter.Mod
.Ed
.Pp
Build a library of two modules, and a program that uses it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ poc -output-dir lib -library shapes Shapes.Mod Areas.Mod
$ poc -library-path lib Main.Mod
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clang 1 ,
.Xr gdb 1 ,
.Xr lldb 1
.Pp
.Em The Peaseblossom User's Guide
.Pq Pa users-guide.md
shows how to use
.Nm ;
.Em The Peaseblossom Reference Guide
.Pq Pa reference-guide.md
gives its exact rules, its extensions and the runtime modules'
interfaces.
Both are installed in the documentation directory.
.Rs
.%A H. M\(:ossenb\(:ock
.%A N. Wirth
.%T The Programming Language Oberon-2
.%I ETH Z\(:urich
.Re
.Sh AUTHORS
.An T. Kurt Bond
.Sh BUGS
An integer
.Ic DIV
or
.Ic MOD
by zero kills the program with
.Dv SIGFPE
on x86, and gives a value on aarch64; neither is checked.
